  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Saved measurements: how to read this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Metrics are backfilled from the saved Docker samples at their **original timestamps**. Select a profile to compare its four variants; select Component to switch API / collector in the first two rows. CPU = percent of one core; memory = Docker working set without inactive file cache. Summary panels use the report's measurement window, not the currently zoomed interval. A summary appears only when its sample timestamp is within the selected time range.\n\nCollector panels are fixed to `component=collector`; load panels are fixed to `component=api`. **Grafana, Prometheus and Tempo were added after the full workload matrix**; their later live resource measurements do not form part of that historical matrix.\n\n[Open Tempo Explore](/explore?schemaVersion=1&panes={%22lab6%22%3A{%22datasource%22%3A%22lab6-tempo%22%2C%22queries%22%3A%5B{%22refId%22%3A%22A%22%2C%22datasource%22%3A{%22type%22%3A%22tempo%22%2C%22uid%22%3A%22lab6-tempo%22}%2C%22queryType%22%3A%22traceql%22%2C%22query%22%3A%22%22}%5D%2C%22range%22%3A{%22from%22%3A%22${__from}%22%2C%22to%22%3A%22${__to}%22}}}): choose **TraceQL**, paste an ID from imported `traces.jsonl`. Example for the saved full run: `__EXAMPLE_TRACE_ID__` (selected imported run). A trace lookup needs an imported trace; an empty search result does not invalidate CPU/RAM samples. Historical spans may be outside Tempo's time-based search window; use Trace ID lookup."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "CPU — selected component (% of one core)",
      "description": "10-second rate of the cumulative CPU-seconds counter. 100% means one fully occupied CPU core.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "lab6-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "rate(lab6_cpu_seconds_total{run=~\"${run:regex}\",profile=~\"${profile:regex}\",variant=~\"${variant:regex}\",repetition=~\"${repetition:regex}\",component=~\"${component:regex}\"}[10s]) * 100",
          "legendFormat": "{{profile}} / {{variant}} / r{{repetition}} / {{component}} / {{run}}",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "lab6-prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "RAM — selected component (MiB)",
      "description": "Samples older than 5 seconds are hidden to avoid Prometheus lookback extending a finished workload.",
